{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\n\nThe `summary` read (src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py, around line 480) calls `deps_state` once per requested id, and each call can rebuild the dependency graph from a full whole-store reduce. Measured on a clone of the live store, 2026-10-29: 3 ids took 29,187 ticket reductions and read 935 MB from disk, with a peak of 284.4 MB per pass.\n\nRe-measured on a fresh copy after humdrum-priestly-lcont merged (6acef632), graph cache removed before each run: 3 ids took 3 whole-store passes and 29,238 ticket reductions (1 id: 1 pass, 9,746), peak 44.8 MB (the trimmed graph load). The repeat comes from `build_dep_graph` (src/rebar/graph/_graph.py): its cache stores graphs per ticket id, so each new id misses and `_compute_dep_graph` calls `load_indexed_states` again. Nothing a summary does changes ticket directories between ids (the graph load uses `exclude_archived=False`, so it heals no markers; only `.graph-cache.json` is written, which the load skips as a dot-file), so the states are the same for every id.\n\nPlan item 2 of the original plan is already true: the per-id fields come from `show_state` without the inbound scan, which reduces only the named ticket directory. It needs no change.\n\n## Plan\n1. Give `build_dep_graph` and `_compute_dep_graph` an optional keyword-only `load_states` callable (internal; `build_dep_graph` is not in the public API surface). When given, a cache miss calls it instead of `load_indexed_states`; a cache hit never calls it.\n2. Thread it through `reads.deps_state` (same optional keyword) and add `gates.summary_many(ticket_ids, tracker)`, which builds one memoised loader (loads at most once, and only if some id misses the cache) and calls `summary_compute(..., load_states=...)` per id. `summary_cli` and the library `rebar.summary` (src/rebar/_lib_gates.py) call `summary_many`; `rebar.summary`'s signature is unchanged.\n3. Tests first, seen failing on current code: with 3 ids and no graph cache, `summary_many` performs exactly one `reduce_all_tickets` call; its output equals the per-id `summary_compute` loop on a multi-id fixture (blocked, ready, archived, unknown and session_log ids); with a warm cache it performs none.\n4. Measure passes, reductions and tracemalloc peak for 3 ids on a store copy before and after, compare outputs, and record them here.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `summary` with 3 ids and no graph cache performs 1 `reduce_all_tickets` call, not 3; verified by a counting test in tests/unit/test_summary_single_graph_load.py and on a store copy.\n- [ ] `summary` output for a multi-id fixture equals the per-id loop's output; verified by the same test module.\n- [ ] Before/after passes, reductions, peak and output equality on a store copy are recorded in a ticket comment.\n\n## File impact (expected)\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py\n- src/rebar/graph/_graph.py\n- src/rebar/_lib_gates.py\n- tests/unit/test_summary_single_graph_load.py"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793317785173263001,"uuid":"c3eaafad-aa91-44f5-b690-f0494c711605"}